{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy","id":1127598,"title":"Mind magic and frenzy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-11T06:39:45-07:00","id":1127598,"title":"Mind magic and frenzy","content":"Since I can't find anywhere a reference to solve or clarify this: when a mage with mind magic (but the same could be applied to a vampire with dominate or presence) gives a command to a subject, if the victim suffers from frenzy, Kuruth, rage or basu im..etc..etc.. Does this &quot;override&quot; the mind control and set them free, or do they still have to obey the mind master since the duration of the spell/command is extended/one scene? <br /> <br /> For example, if I use mind magic and command a gangrel to stop and stand still, if by any chance he goes into frenzy Will he break free from mind magic? <br /> Same issue with a werewolf and rage or death rage. <br /> <br /> Thanks to anyone that will help cheers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T06:52:43-07:00","id":1127602,"title":"","content":"The werewolf possibly will, but for a very strange reason: Assuming they were commanded in human form, entering kuruth will cause them to become larger. If the mage didn't increase the scale factor when they cast the spell to cover things up to size 7, this will mean the spell will stop working on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:01:43-07:00","id":1127638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127602#post1127602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The werewolf possibly will, but for a very strange reason: Assuming they were commanded in human form, entering kuruth will cause them to become larger. If the mage didn't increase the scale factor when they cast the spell to cover things up to size 7, this will mean the spell will stop working on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow I honestly never thought about that do size factors matter even with an abstract concept like mind? I thought size factor was meant for &quot;real&quot; and solid things like matter corpses and living beings, or spirits and ghosts... <br /> Maybe the werewolf thoughts and mind become.. Bigger? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Anyway Raw u might be right I need to re read that paragraph","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:18:06-07:00","id":1127651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127638#post1127638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow I honestly never thought about that do size factors matter even with an abstract concept like mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>As the recent discussion about Area Scale has helped to underline, even if what they affect are notionally abstract things, spells themselves are not; a spell made to encompass a Size 5 being cannot maintain its effect usefully if the target then becomes Size 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:21:53-07:00","id":1127755,"title":"","content":"It's actually mentioned in the vampire book a bit. Dominate can direct the vampire's frenzy at another target, but it can't bring them out of it, or give them no target.<br /> <br /> Animalism also allows control over a frenzy-ing vampire, and there are some devotions of animalism to dampen the predatory aura but I don't think there is anything to end it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:42:57-07:00","id":1127853,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think dominate would have trouble controlling a werewolf in Kuruth. You're basically giving their rational mind instructions, but their rational mind is all &quot;buddy, I'm not driving right now&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T19:59:32-07:00","id":1127897,"title":"","content":"The Mind arcana on the other hand can skip past the rational mind. Theoretically, one option is for a Mind Mage in a Hallow to rip out the goetia that represents the frenzy, it'd probably spiritually (or otherwise) cripple the werewolf or vampire since that aspect of their mind would be effectively removed from their mental makeup. You'd also have a frenzied goetia on your hands. Of course that would only work -if- the frenzy they experience is just a mental state. Whether or not it is, is in my opinion one of those questions for the ST to decide, but the results could be interesting either way. Again, theoretically, Life could calm a frenzy though it'd only work for werewolves, flood them with whatever hormones you need to calm something down, bam, no more frenzy. That does still fall into the realm of, -if- a frenzy is purely a function of the brain. Given vampires don't really have functioning brains and that werewolves don't really have fully physical brains I think I'd rule it as reaching some kind of halfway state where they need to attack, but can consciously cooperate with tricks or traps from others (Including consciously going after valid targets), that take advantage of that need, to prevent them from doing something they'll regret (more) when they come out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T21:32:57-07:00","id":1127911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127853#post1127853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think dominate would have trouble controlling a werewolf in Kuruth. You're basically giving their rational mind instructions, but their rational mind is all &amp;quot;buddy, I'm not driving right now&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nevermind how difficult it'd be holding a Gauru's gaze while they are trying to eat you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127897#post1127897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mind arcana on the other hand can skip past the rational mind. Theoretically, one option is for a Mind Mage in a Hallow to rip out the goetia that represents the frenzy, it'd probably spiritually (or otherwise) cripple the werewolf or vampire since that aspect of their mind would be effectively removed from their mental makeup. You'd also have a frenzied goetia on your hands. Of course that would only work -if- the frenzy they experience is just a mental state. Whether or not it is, is in my opinion one of those questions for the ST to decide, but the results could be interesting either way. Again, theoretically, Life could calm a frenzy though it'd only work for werewolves, flood them with whatever hormones you need to calm something down, bam, no more frenzy. That does still fall into the realm of, -if- a frenzy is purely a function of the brain. Given vampires don't really have functioning brains and that werewolves don't really have fully physical brains I think I'd rule it as reaching some kind of halfway state where they need to attack, but can consciously cooperate with tricks or traps from others (Including consciously going after valid targets), that take advantage of that need, to prevent them from doing something they'll regret (more) when they come out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would still face a penalty equal to twice the Uratha's primal urge, on top of any other factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T21:38:55-07:00","id":1127915,"title":"","content":"First off thank you all for ur replies, and from now on I will consider scale factors also for mind and abstract arcana. Second, I wanted to ask u about werewolf rage specifically.<br /> It is stated in the werewolf rules for rage that &quot;<br /> any attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the <br /> Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer <br /> twice the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge as a penalty. This is over and above <br /> any Supernatural Tolerance (p. 160) applied to supernatural powers&quot;<br /> <br /> So I guess that a vampire or a mind mage will have an hard time trying to stop the raging beast since at primal urge 2 for example they will subtract 4 dices to their gnosis Arcanum or dominate pools... <br /> <br /> But what about a werewolf that was already dominated / mind enslaved BEFORE the rage? <br /> Will the command still be in place, or will the kuruth primal urge penalty call for a clash of wills or a reroll of the power? <br /> <br /> To make a clear example, if a mind mage spent the necessary reaches winning the whitstand of the shapeshifter, and made the werewolf freeze in place for the entire scene, if by any means that same wolf enters in basu im or kuruth later he will remain paralyzed anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T23:13:53-07:00","id":1127939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127915#post1127915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off thank you all for ur replies, and from now on I will consider scale factors also for mind and abstract arcana. Second, I wanted to ask u about werewolf rage specifically.<br /> It is stated in the werewolf rules for rage that &amp;quot;<br /> any attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the <br /> Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer <br /> twice the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge as a penalty. This is over and above <br /> any Supernatural Tolerance (p. 160) applied to supernatural powers&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So I guess that a vampire or a mind mage will have an hard time trying to stop the raging beast since at primal urge 2 for example they will subtract 4 dices to their gnosis Arcanum or dominate pools... <br /> <br /> But what about a werewolf that was already dominated / mind enslaved BEFORE the rage? <br /> Will the command still be in place, or will the kuruth primal urge penalty call for a clash of wills or a reroll of the power? <br /> <br /> To make a clear example, if a mind mage spent the necessary reaches winning the whitstand of the shapeshifter, and made the werewolf freeze in place for the entire scene, if by any means that same wolf enters in basu im or kuruth later he will remain paralyzed anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends: Did the freeze spell hampered the Uratha's sensory imput to the point that nothing can trigger it? Ot did some Elodoth switched that rage on? IMO, no rage if the scenario 1 is as I suspect, yes to scenario 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T00:25:31-07:00","id":1127957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127939#post1127939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends: Did the freeze spell hampered the Uratha's sensory imput to the point that nothing can trigger it? Ot did some Elodoth switched that rage on? IMO, no rage if the scenario 1 is as I suspect, yes to scenario 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to be more specific. <br /> Let's say that I'm a desperate mastigos confronted by a werewolf and cornered. I use mind magic to dominate him with psychic domination and spend extra reach for size and type of command and i tell him to &quot;freeze don't move no matter what&quot;. <br /> An Elodoth see the mage working his curse and his companion mind blocked, so he uses his powers to cause him to rage hoping to free him from the spell. <br /> <br /> Another case, the werewolf simply remains frozen in place under the spell command, the wizard calmly pulls out a silver bullet loaded gun and shoot the werewolf in the head. Will this break the spell and set the werewolf free to act and frenzy attacking the mage? <br /> <br /> The problem is that as Raw there is no mention of combat or damage or frenzy as spell breaking factors.. So the werewolf would simply frenzy and stay still while the mage shoots his bullets. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, one could argue that the werewolf simply cannot control himself so he cannot follow the command he was given during his previous state, since now is mind is completely overrun by irrational urge to destroy... <br /> <br /> Personally as a storyteller I would alow frenzy or kuruth or rage as mind /dominate control breakers, possibly with a clash of wills","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T00:53:23-07:00","id":1127959,"title":"","content":"I, personally, feel that were I the werewolf entering frenzy in this situation, I would be filled with the deepest most hate ridden rage imaginable, amped up to 11, towards the object of my frenzy. Unfortunately, because I am also supernaturally compelled not to move, I would not be able to move. But I would really, <i>really</i> want to. Being trapped in that kind of situation would be a psychological nightmare. However - if I recall, there -are- possible measures of control. You can postpone frenzy, you can enact it, or quell it - and you can direct it. None of these are easy - sometimes requiring the investment of merits or willpower, but in many cases they are possible. The Frenzy does not supernaturally compel you to move - it does however fill you with a supernatural, inescapable, rage - or fear, in some vampire's cases. That rage has consequences, and that is why you must move - because you are beyond the concept of anger, and suddenly rage incarnate. Your <i>emotion</i> causes your reactions. Unfortunately, the mage's commands do not tie into your emotion. He is not instilling in you a desire to remain still - he is giving you a command and you must obey. Were he to create a calm area around himself preventing you from having the will to attack, entering frenzy would provoke a clash of wills - but without that, I would say no - you're stuck.<br /> <br /> In the case of the werewolf vs the Mind Mage with the Silver Gun - this depends. Did the Mage spend reach in order to allow the commands to be suicidal? If not, then the command is suddenly suicidal and does not need to be followed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T00:55:56-07:00","id":1127960,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not sure if by raw they should break out, but having a werewolf in kuruth just standing there seems... wrong. <br /> <br /> &quot;Stand still no matter what&quot;<br /> &quot;I'm sorry, that didn't sound like 'indiscriminately murder everything in reach', try again.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:00:46-07:00","id":1127961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127959#post1127959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, personally, feel that were I the werewolf entering frenzy in this situation, I would be filled with the deepest most hate ridden rage imaginable, amped up to 11, towards the object of my frenzy. Unfortunately, because I am also supernaturally compelled not to move, I would not be able to move. But I would really, <i>really</i> want to. Being trapped in that kind of situation would be a psychological nightmare. However - if I recall, there -are- possible measures of control. You can postpone frenzy, you can enact it, or quell it - and you can direct it. None of these are easy - sometimes requiring the investment of merits or willpower, but in many cases they are possible. The Frenzy does not supernaturally compel you to move - it does however fill you with a supernatural, inescapable, rage - or fear, in some vampire's cases. That rage has consequences, and that is why you must move - because you are beyond the concept of anger, and suddenly rage incarnate. Your <i>emotion</i> causes your reactions. Unfortunately, the mage's commands do not tie into your emotion. He is not instilling in you a desire to remain still - he is giving you a command and you must obey. Were he to create a calm area around himself preventing you from having the will to attack, entering frenzy would provoke a clash of wills - but without that, I would say no - you're stuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Uratha in basu-im who decidedly takes on his killing form and thus triggers wasu-im has no actual recognizable though process or understanding of the concept &quot;to remain quiet&quot; as far as I know. There is no way the issued command would be understood after all reason escapes the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:18:38-07:00","id":1127970,"title":"","content":"I agree that a werewolf in full basu Im who stands still while getting shot at doesn't make sense that's why even if there is no mention I would allow for a clash of wills at least as St. <br /> <br /> Problem is that raw there is nothing stopping a mind mage from mind enslaving frenzy vampires and kuruth werewolves.<br /> <br /> Maybe the core of the debate and that should redifine the problem is &quot;does mind totally override both the conscious and unconscious mind (and the beast and rage too), and do the frenzy beast and basu im processes involve chemical brain, conscious or unconscious thoughts, or pure supernatural&quot; magic'??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:25:33-07:00","id":1127971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127961#post1127961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Uratha in basu-im who decidedly takes on his killing form and thus triggers wasu-im has no actual recognizable though process or understanding of the concept &quot;to remain quiet&quot; as far as I know. There is no way the issued command would be understood after all reason escapes the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is of my personal opinion that if this were the case, then instead of applying a penalty based upon primal urge to create effects that run counter to the actions of the Frenzy, that they would instead simply negate them. Even in the midst of frenzy, it is not impossible to command a wolf to stay still - however, it is certainly harder to make the spell stick. With that in mind, this situation gives an example where the spell has 'already' stuck. It's kind of similar to putting a helmet on after getting hit in the head - or, if I were to use mage terms, it'd be similar to applying a mind shield after the command to remain still had been given.<br /> <br /> Does this seem wrong? Absolutely. A werewolf should never be still in the middle of Kuruth. But just because it <i>seems</i> wrong doesn't mean that it's not the way that works or even not the way it -should- work. A Kuruth frozen solid by a mental command going to be very -clearly- seen as being held down by some mystical force by any individual who recognizes the Death Rage for what it is. And by Luna, if it's not going to be one of the strangest, creepiest, or otherwise most alien thing that any wolf who succeeds in not entering the Death Rage has ever seen - simply because to them, the idea that that is even possible <i>feels wrong</i>.<br /> <br /> Edit: Weirdly enough though, apply this same concept to a vampire and RAW you have a different story. They -do- negate the effects of social and mystical effects to cause them to act in a way contrary to their Beast. Hm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 08-12-2017, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:30:42-07:00","id":1127972,"title":"","content":"Again: You cannot follow a command which you cannot possibly understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:41:16-07:00","id":1127976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127972#post1127972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: You cannot follow a command which you cannot possibly understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have to? Your subconscious understands and locks down the body. Whether you consciously get it yourself is irrelevant. I don't think Mind magic necessarily booms a voice in your head &quot;Hey, stand still! Ok?&quot; and then rely on you obeying that voice either, so understanding seems wholly irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:55:31-07:00","id":1127977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127972#post1127972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: You cannot follow a command which you cannot possibly understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be totally 100 per cent with you on this, IF we were talking about dominate. <br /> <br /> The problem with mind magic and with magic in general is that you completely rewrite the associated element of reality to suit your needs. <br /> <br /> When a mage issue a command with mind magic he doesn't simply says a command to you, he rewrites your mind so that you obey him effectively controlling your mind directly and gaining complete control over your concept of mind and thought. <br /> <br /> Language and understandable words or commands do not apply in my opinion to mind magic, since mind magic has purview over PURE THOUGHT and not just commands or suggestions. This is why there's an issue for me whether mind completely overrun any and all thoughts processes or it simply works like dominate and presence. <br /> <br /> If mind has really purview over any thoughts and mental impulse or command regardless of language barriers or emotions, then it defeats kuruth and frenzy as well. Which it could as well be the case, since we are talking about pure mind and not simply instructions to follow. <br /> <br /> While I do agree that a raging wolf shouldn't be stopped with a simple command previously issued, I see that that might ad well be the case Raw. I as a storyteller, would try to settle this with possibly a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T02:09:39-07:00","id":1127981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127977#post1127977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be totally 100 per cent with you on this, IF we were talking about dominate.<br /> <br /> The problem with mind magic and with magic in general is that you completely rewrite the associated element of reality to suit your needs.<br /> <br /> When a mage issue a command with mind magic he doesn't simply says a command to you, he rewrites your mind so that you obey him effectively controlling your mind directly and gaining complete control over your concept of mind and thought.<br /> <br /> Language and understandable words or commands do not apply in my opinion to mind magic, since mind magic has purview over PURE THOUGHT and not just commands or suggestions. This is why there's an issue for me whether mind completely overrun any and all thoughts processes or it simply works like dominate and presence.<br /> <br /> If mind has really purview over any thoughts and mental impulse or command regardless of language barriers or emotions, then it defeats kuruth and frenzy as well. Which it could as well be the case, since we are talking about pure mind and not simply instructions to follow.<br /> <br /> While I do agree that a raging wolf shouldn't be stopped with a simple command previously issued, I see that that might ad well be the case Raw. I as a storyteller, would try to settle this with possibly a clash of wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* I can definitely see a case of house ruling this to be effective. When you consider the fact that the Vampiric Frenzy -does- prevent supernatural tamperings that go against their nature, it's quite possible that werewolf simply didn't address it because the game line doesn't have the ability to cause an individual to go against their nature with any particular gift. On the other hand, it's legit harder to avoid vampiric frenzy than it is Kuruth - so some games might qualify vampire's type of frenzy to be 'stronger' (a strange thought to me, to be sure).<br /> <br /> While there is something to be said about the raw horror that one might feel when they try to cause their packmate to frenzy and they still remain still, there is certainly nothing wrong with applying a clash of wills if you feel that's appropriate (especially if it's PvP - you want to be as fair as possible after all and give all players a fighting chance). If I applied this however, I would make a note that the clash is not against the frenzy itself, but against a supernatural compulsion caused by the frenzy to move and kill. In other words, if the mage wins and then later drops his spell, or the duration runs out: Bye bye everyone and everything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T02:24:36-07:00","id":1127984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127977#post1127977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be totally 100 per cent with you on this, IF we were talking about dominate. <br /> <br /> The problem with mind magic and with magic in general is that you completely rewrite the associated element of reality to suit your needs. <br /> <br /> When a mage issue a command with mind magic he doesn't simply says a command to you, he rewrites your mind so that you obey him effectively controlling your mind directly and gaining complete control over your concept of mind and thought. <br /> <br /> Language and understandable words or commands do not apply in my opinion to mind magic, since mind magic has purview over PURE THOUGHT and not just commands or suggestions. This is why there's an issue for me whether mind completely overrun any and all thoughts processes or it simply works like dominate and presence. <br /> <br /> If mind has really purview over any thoughts and mental impulse or command regardless of language barriers or emotions, then it defeats kuruth and frenzy as well. Which it could as well be the case, since we are talking about pure mind and not simply instructions to follow. <br /> <br /> While I do agree that a raging wolf shouldn't be stopped with a simple command previously issued, I see that that might ad well be the case Raw. I as a storyteller, would try to settle this with possibly a clash of wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept of thought isn't available to a uratha in the throes of Kuruth, or even in much of non-Death Raging Gauru.<br /> <br /> That's why it's called Death Rage in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-12-2017, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T03:20:35-07:00","id":1127995,"title":"","content":"I agree partially with you, and see what you mean. But it is not totally true that the concept of thought isn't available to an uratha in rage, otherwise it wouldn't be possible to influence or manipulate a raging uratha , and thus the paragraph where they wrote about the penalty for commanding a raging uratha wouldn't need to exist,<br /> Rage and the impulse of killing everything and everyone is a thought and an impulse, even if primordial and difficult to manipulate. (i quote from the book: <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">any attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">twice the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge as a penalty.</span>&quot;)&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">So it's probably possible to influence, intimidate and change the uratha course of actions, it's just very hard.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another objection i have to point out is that, (maybe words and meanings are confusing here)- Mind doesn't simply control thoughts emotions and processes, it pbobably control the very same Will of a being. <br /> <br /> Even if an uratha in basu im has no rational thought process, while in frenzy he still has to use his brain to focus his&quot;will&quot; on the act of destruction, and then giving the brain command to his muscles and reflexes to kill the prey. Mind has purview over basically anything that comes from the same very concept of Mind and brain, and consequently any kind of &quot;will&quot; to destroy, run, attack or anything.<br /> <br /> mind control the very same electric signals sent to your neurons that make u able to think, see, act and move. That'ts how thought and will work.<br /> <br /> What i'm trying to say here is that mind comes BEFORE the command and the thinking. It gets inside your very will to think and exists, and THEN it gets the work done, effectively rewriting your very same willpower.<br /> Mind manipulate and control basic impulses and intent , it doesn't need to elaborate on complex thoughts and commands or conditions. (althought if necesary it can do that too)<br /> <br /> If we consider that even a basu im war form uratha needs at very least a basic level of instinct to kill and will and needs to think and command his muscles and eyes to move, then Mind can impose himself on that too, thus rendering the werewolf unable to act even while in rage.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T04:58:35-07:00","id":1128008,"title":"","content":"Is this because 2 players are using powers on each other or something? Cos if not i think you are thinking way to hard about it and just need to decide whats best for the story you wanna tell.<br /> If its 2 players, one mage &amp; one Werewolf then kek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T05:38:47-07:00","id":1128020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127911#post1127911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would still face a penalty equal to twice the Uratha's primal urge, on top of any other factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Difficulty of the task doesn't have much if anything to do with what I posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T07:38:13-07:00","id":1128041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128008#post1128008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this because 2 players are using powers on each other or something? Cos if not i think you are thinking way to hard about it and just need to decide whats best for the story you wanna tell.<br /> If its 2 players, one mage &amp; one Werewolf then kek.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was being a little bit philosophically nerd for the sake of debate and for fun, but yeah I still stand for a very simple and elegant clash of wills <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:52:52-07:00","id":1128110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1127897#post1127897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mind arcana on the other hand can skip past the rational mind. Theoretically, one option is for a Mind Mage in a Hallow to rip out the goetia that represents the frenzy, it'd probably spiritually (or otherwise) cripple the werewolf or vampire since that aspect of their mind would be effectively removed from their mental makeup. You'd also have a frenzied goetia on your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves Dave said that werewolves, vampires, and basically any splat that isn't human or a mage doesn't have an Oneiros. So, would there even be a Goetia that represented the Beast in vampires or a Werewolf's death rage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:08:10-07:00","id":1128119,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, he did.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so goetia removal ain't gonna work here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:33:31-07:00","id":1128161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128110#post1128110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If memory serves Dave said that werewolves, vampires, and basically any splat that isn't human or a mage doesn't have an Oneiros. So, would there even be a Goetia that represented the Beast in vampires or a Werewolf's death rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Well, that's just one method, Mind would still work on some level I imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:52:13-07:00","id":1128168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128161#post1128161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. Well, that's just one method, Mind would still work on some level I imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine on some level it would work. I haven't run a mage chronicle yet, and I imagine we'll get some answers at some point in a supplement book or something.<br /> <br /> Though depending on the ST they might let Death work on ripping out a Vampire's Beast or Spirit to bring a werewolf out of death rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:57:33-07:00","id":1128207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128168#post1128168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine on some level it would work. I haven't run a mage chronicle yet, and I imagine we'll get some answers at some point in a supplement book or something.<br /> <br /> Though depending on the ST they might let Death work on ripping out a Vampire's Beast or Spirit to bring a werewolf out of death rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fundamentally screwing with a template like that requires archmastery on the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:39:00-07:00","id":1128310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128207#post1128207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fundamentally screwing with a template like that requires archmastery on the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need death five to rip out template souls, and the Beast is definitely a part of the vampire's soul.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure you'd need Archmastery just to stop a werewolf from death raging at that point in time, not forever and always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T11:33:42-07:00","id":1128524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128310#post1128310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need death five to rip out template souls, and the Beast is definitely a part of the vampire's soul.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure you'd need Archmastery just to stop a werewolf from death raging at that point in time, not forever and always.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast isn't the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T11:36:04-07:00","id":1128525,"title":"","content":"Also it might not be a good idea to pull out the Beast, lest you find yourself possessed by an owl-shaped cloud of smoke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T11:44:22-07:00","id":1128527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128524#post1128524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Beast isn't the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of it, no. It's definitely an aspect of a vampiric soul though. Even if they tore out the soul, the vampire will have a lot more problems than a non-functioning Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T11:53:07-07:00","id":1128529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128310#post1128310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need death five to rip out template souls, and the Beast is definitely a part of the vampire's soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need Death 5 to rip out Awakened souls. Other altered souls has no official rules. Also, altering non-Mage templates is still Archmaster territory, which I believe should extend to ripping souls out of them. Also, there's nothing confirming that the Beast is part of the vampire's analogue for a soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:40:25-07:00","id":1128596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128529#post1128529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need Death 5 to rip out Awakened souls. Other altered souls has no official rules. Also, altering non-Mage templates is still Archmaster territory, which I believe should extend to ripping souls out of them. Also, there's nothing confirming that the Beast is part of the vampire's analogue for a soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I thought it was on the forum or something that other template souls were similar to awakened souls when it came to death five ripping them out. Must've been a thing my st decided was the case for our game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:57:46-07:00","id":1128604,"title":"","content":"Beast has rules for it, in regards to their template, that involve using Death 5 rather than 3 - but mechanically most other splats don't get explicitly called out the way they did in 1e. That may, however, simply be because they don't yet have the supplement book which expresses that.They definately imply it though, with the writeup involving the tremere in thousand years of night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T16:32:28-07:00","id":1128610,"title":"","content":"Getting rid of a werewolf's rage might not be the best idea, since then you would have a werewolf who can go into gauru indefinitely without a drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T17:10:57-07:00","id":1128624,"title":"","content":"I wouldnt allow removing a vampires beast/WW's rage without imperial magic, is basically template modification?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T19:56:39-07:00","id":1128684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128604#post1128604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast has rules for it, in regards to their template, that involve using Death 5 rather than 3 - but mechanically most other splats don't get explicitly called out the way they did in 1e. That may, however, simply be because they don't yet have the supplement book which expresses that.They definately imply it though, with the writeup involving the tremere in thousand years of night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, the Tremere were in 1000 years of night? Where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T20:07:49-07:00","id":1128688,"title":"","content":"In the mage section under Crossovers. It's implied there's a mage who's using vampires to keep from aging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T20:09:38-07:00","id":1128689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128684#post1128684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, the Tremere were in 1000 years of night? Where?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crossover section. Dominic ought to be in his nineties, but doesn't look a day over forty and has been missing his aura for years; people around him tend to go missing, and if they turn up later they're shells of their former selves. He visited the piece's narrator's estate months ago and took a list of the vampire's associates; their childe has since disappeared from correspondence for weeks.<br /> <br /> There's other ways to read that, admittedly, but, knowing the conceptual overlap between diablerie and regular magical soul-eating, it's sufficiently up in the air to make a plot hook out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:19:02-07:00","id":1130235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1128596#post1128596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I thought it was on the forum or something that other template souls were similar to awakened souls when it came to death five ripping them out. Must've been a thing my st decided was the case for our game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1010803#post1010803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not only wrong, but Beasts' corebook clearly says what happens. The mage has to use Death 5, but mages <i>can</i> steal Beasts' souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>It causes the immediate death of the Beast when you rip out their Horror in this way. Note that this was discussed in a few other posts as well, this was just the first one I found.<br /> <br /> It follows, though it isn't explicit, that other supernaturals can have their 'souls' stripped away in the exact same manner. What their soul equivalents are is up for debate, however.<br /> <br /> Also, the whole 'not fucking with other templates below archmastery' bit - is that actually explicit in 2E anywhere? I remember it from 1E, but more than a few things that were archmastery in 1E aren't anymore, and the whole 'ripping out a Beast's Horror' thing seems to directly contradict it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:35:34-07:00","id":1130248,"title":"","content":"That isn't altering the Beast's powers, though, it's just killing him in a particularly over-the-top way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:42:51-07:00","id":1130255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130248#post1130248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't altering the Beast's powers, though, it's just killing him in a particularly over-the-top way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, but removing a Changeling's soul, for example, would (probably?) have more direct affects on their abilities than just killing them.<br /> <br /> Would doing so be impossible, then? <br /> <br /> Or to rephrase - is the reason it works for Beasts <i>because</i> it kills them while not meaningfully interfering with their template? Therefore in cases where it would cause such interference, Mages are unable to remove their souls using the same methods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T10:13:43-07:00","id":1130337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130255#post1130255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair, but removing a Changeling's soul, for example, would (probably?) have more direct affects on their abilities than just killing them.<br /> <br /> Would doing so be impossible, then?<br /> <br /> Or to rephrase - is the reason it works for Beasts <i>because</i> it kills them while not meaningfully interfering with their template? Therefore in cases where it would cause such interference, Mages are unable to remove their souls using the same methods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thorns already took care of the helpless former mortal's soul anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T10:21:05-07:00","id":1130340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130235#post1130235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It causes the immediate death of the Beast when you rip out their Horror in this way. Note that this was discussed in a few other posts as well, this was just the first one I found.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you get that. The Beast book, where it covers this, doesn't mention the Beast dying when it happens, only that it's difficult to do.<br /> <br /> 'Worst of all are mages who steal the souls of victims for use in experiments or fuel for strange powers; a Beast\u2019s soul is a difficult but prestigious prize for so-called \u201cReapers.\u201d Due to Beast\u2019s connection to their Lair mages can\u2019t steal the soul of a Begotten just by casting a spell in the physical world. It requires as much ability with the Arcana as taking the soul of a mage, and can only be cast inside the Lair. Despite the risks, some Reapers who learn the existence of Beasts go on twisted safaris into the Primordial Pathways, convinced that they can reduce the Children of the Dark Mother to big game.'<br /> <br /> It seems like if it killed the character it would mention that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It follows, though it isn't explicit, that other supernaturals can have their 'souls' stripped away in the exact same manner. What their soul equivalents are is up for debate, however. </div> </div> </div>Yes, idigam rip the souls out of things as a matter of course, it's practically a hobby. It doesn't mean death to the supernaturals involved. We've examples of soulless supernaturals in the books, and soullessness alone doesn't seem to equal death to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T10:58:00-07:00","id":1130352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130340#post1130340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure where you get that.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the dev that I quoted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:00:15-07:00","id":1130353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130352#post1130352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the dev that I quoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I'm not seeing a quote aside from Dave Brookshaw's, which doesn't say the Beast dies. Could you link it?<br /> <br /> It seems like you would get an Unfettered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:10:15-07:00","id":1130356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130248#post1130248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't altering the Beast's powers, though, it's just killing him in a particularly over-the-top way.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> it was on the previous page of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:18:32-07:00","id":1130362,"title":"","content":"My display is set to 40 posts per page. But it seems like Inodiv posted about it killing the Beast before Dave posted.<br /> <br /> It's fine to go that way but I'd really ask for clarification from Dave, especially considering he didn't quote any particular line when saying that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:16:34-07:00","id":1130394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130362#post1130362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My display is set to 40 posts per page. But it seems like Inodiv posted about it killing the Beast before Dave posted.<br /> <br /> It's fine to go that way but I'd really ask for clarification from Dave, especially considering he didn't quote any particular line when saying that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Horror explicitly can't be forced to leave the Lair outside the bounds of its hunting and takes the Beast with it if it's killed; the only normal circumstances in which a Beast is concretely separated from its Horror are the ones that lead to the Retreat, which sets a rather more brutal precedent than falling to soullessness typically entails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:30:14-07:00","id":1130404,"title":"","content":"So other means of stealing souls just outright kills the Beast too? Not everyone has it as hard as mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:34:34-07:00","id":1130407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130404#post1130404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So other means of stealing souls just outright kills the Beast too? Not everyone has it as hard as mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other means of stealing souls are likely subject to the same sort of restrictions, because when your soul is a piece of the collective unconscious it tends to have inertia on its side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:37:02-07:00","id":1130409,"title":"","content":"Okay that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:53:06-07:00","id":1130506,"title":"","content":"Huh. Look at that. The &quot;and is fatal to the Beast&quot; got cut off the line somewhere in the Writing -&gt; Book process. <br /> <br /> Never mind that, then - you probably just get an Unfettered!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachm