"title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T10:20:26-07:00","id":1130880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130843#post1130843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Does not apply in this case, where is the other power?</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> sorry for maybe going OT (or maybe going back on topic on the main issue regarding the beginning of the post) <br /> and i usually don't want to bother the gameline creators since i guess u guys always receive messages and get asked questions all the time\u2026<br /> <br /> But how would you personally rule the clash between dominate/ mind magic control / and frenzy/rage/basu im? In your opinion, does werewolf rage/ vampire frenzy beast \u201coverride\u201d psychic domination commands, or will the mind influence still works on a blood driven undead/shapeshifter?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m asking that since u wanted to intervene in the discussion and now i have a chance to ask your opinion straight away, hoping to get your insight on this\u2026 <br /> <br /> <br /> ps- i also wanted to say thank you and really appreciate your work and effort on this gameline, you have no idea how many fun nights me and my friends had playing this awesome awakened game experience , you just got yourself a misteries addicted cabal from italy! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T21:03:36-07:00","id":1131112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1127598-mind-magic-and-frenzy?p=1130843#post1130843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Does not apply in this case, where is the other power?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying, if it were my gaming table and something like that pops out, having both sides a sound position, I'd just adjudicate a Clash of Wills roll between the spell and an ad hoc dice pool for the Basu Im state, for example Resolve + Primal Urge. Death Rage is not technically a power, that is correct, but it could be considered a power nonetheless for the purpose of resolving a clash of supernatural properties between two different types of creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}